>> title: Baked Pork Chop Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: pork, rice, tomato, cheese, hong kong, oven
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: guk jyu paa faan, 焗豬扒飯, baked pork chop rice, baked pork chop over rice, Baked Pork Chop Over Spaghetti, pork chop rice
>> pairs-with: egg-fried-rice, homemade-ketchup, pork-chop-in-tomato-sauce
>> servings: 2
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — the chop is cooked before it goes in and the bake is only browning the top, so past fifteen minutes the pork dries out and no amount of sauce brings it back
>> step.1: pound thin, season, rest 20 min
>> step.2: fry 6 min, both sides
>> step.3: simmer the sauce 8 min, until it coats a spoon
>> step.4: fry the rice 4 min, egg through it
>> step.5: layer rice, chop, sauce, cheese — bake 425°F (220°C) 12 min

Pound @boneless pork chops{2}(6 oz each; to 1/2 in) and rub them with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @white pepper{1/2%tsp}, @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs} and @cornstarch{1%Tbs}, then ~rest{20%min}.

Fry @&(~1)pork chops{} in @neutral oil{1%Tbs} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{6%min}, turning once, and lift them onto a board to rest.

Simmer @yellow onion{1/2}(sliced thin), @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @canned chopped tomatoes{7%oz}(200 g), @ketchup{1/3%cup}(80 g), @sugar{2%tsp} and @Worcestershire sauce{2%tsp} in a #saucepan{} for ~simmer{8%min}, until it coats a spoon.

Fry @cold cooked jasmine rice{3%cups}(450 g; day-old) with @eggs{2%large} in @neutral oil{2%tsp} in a #wok{} for ~fry{4%min}, breaking the clumps and turning the egg through it.

Spread @&(~1)fried rice{} in a #baking dish{}, lay @&(~3)pork chops{} over it, flood with @&(~2)tomato sauce{}, cover with @mild cheddar{3%oz}(85 g; grated) and ~bake{12%min} at 425°F (220°C) until the top browns in patches.
